            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/tcbh/hww055</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article explores the relationship between emotions, space and politics in 1980s London, using the Greater London Council, childcare, and racial harassment as particular foci. It brings together political history, the history of emotions, and geography to offer a new way of thinking about political culture, as well as contributing to the history of the 1980s. It is based upon archival sources.</AbstractText>
